From 68598f51a384b89595a7eb7b11130d314f680863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clifford Swartz <cliffordswartz1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:46:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/57] hw/misc: PIC32CM JH/MC DAC (U2214), read back by the
 ADC

One 10-bit channel converting at once on a DATA write (LEFTADJ), against
INTREF (SUPC VREF), VDDANA or VREFA; CTRLB.EOEN drives VOUT (PA02), whose
voltage the "vout" property gives (-1 while not driven) for front
ends; STATUS.READY while enabled. VOUT is ADC0 AIN0 on these parts: the
U2247 ADC reads the DAC there while it drives the pin, and its DAC
reference is the DAC's output. Checked on PIC32CM MC00 silicon
(firmware/hello APP=dac): linear over 0-1023, INTREF full scale 1.02 V,
READY at once. New dac_u2214 overlay; regenerated tables.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted; not for submission to upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
